WEBVTT

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.800
Back in 1835, Samuel
Colt made a special gun.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.950
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.250
The Colt is gone, and it
seems pretty damn likely

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.850
That the demon is behind all of this.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.950
Whoops.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.850
Crossroads are where pacts are made.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.550
In selling your soul, rituals like this,

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.250
You got to put your own
photo into the mix, right?

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.750
I know all about you, Dean Winchester.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.850
I'm looking for the best and brightest.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.250
I'm Sam. I'm Jake.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.950
This is a competition.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.050
Only one of you crazy kids

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.750
Is gonna make it out of here alive.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:15.850
Unh!

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.650
You're tough, you're
smart, you're well-Trained.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.400
Sam, you're my favorite.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.050
Sam! Dean!

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.350
Sam, look out!

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:26.850
Unh!

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.050
No!

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.250
Sam!!

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:01.550
Dean?

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.150
Brought you this back.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.150
No, thanks. I'm fine.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.450
You should eat something.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.050
I said I'm fine.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.150
Dean...

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.250
I hate to bring this up. I really do.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.850
But don't you think maybe it's time...

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.050
We bury Sam?

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:42.750
No.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.300
We could maybe...

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.350
What -- Torch
his corpse?

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:54.250
Not yet.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.250
I want you to come with me.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.250
I'm not going anywhere.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.750
Dean, please.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.450
Won't you cut me some slack?

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.450
I just don't think you
should be alone, that's all.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.250
I got to admit -- I
could use your help.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.250
Something big
is going down --

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.850
End-Of-The-World
big.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.200
Well, then let it end!

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.350
You don't mean that.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.150
You don't think so?

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:27.950
Huh?

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.950
You don't think I've given enough?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.450
You don't think I've paid enough?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.150
I'm done with it.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.650
All of it.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.250
And if you know what's good for you,

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.950
Turn around and get
the hell out of here.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.250
Go!!

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:57.850
I'm sorry.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.450
I'm sorry.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.650
Please just go.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:17.250
You know where I'll be.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:55.750
Howdy, Jake.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.850
I'm -- I'm
dreaming, aren't I?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.450
I got a genius on my hands.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.450
Well, congratulations, Jake.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.450
You're it --
Last man standing.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.650
The american idol.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:14.950
I have to
admit --

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.150
You weren't the horse I was betting on,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.950
But still, I got to give it to you.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.450
Go... to hell.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.550
Been there, done that.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.350
Everything you
put me through --

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.350
Dragging me to that place,

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:30.950
Making me kill those people...

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.950
All part of the beauty pageant.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.150
Jake, I needed the
strongest, and that's you.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.750
Needed me for what?

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.750
Oh, I got a laundry list
of tasty things for you.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.750
The only thing I'm gonna do

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.650
Is wake up, hunt you down,

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.550
And kill you myself.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.550
You know, others have tried.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:52.950
It's not easy.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.050
Trust me, Jake. You want to
be a good little soldier here.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.550
And if I'm not?

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.850
If you're a bad little soldier,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.050
Well, that dear old mom of yours,

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.350
That adorable little sister...

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.750
I'll make certain that
they both live long enough

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:15.050
To know the chewy taste

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.550
Of their own intestines.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.050
No, Jake.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.350
I'm not bluffing.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.650
What do you want me to do?

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.350
Like I said
-- Genius.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.350
You know, when
we were little --

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.950
You couldn't have
been more than 5 --

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.850
You just started asking questions.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.450
How come we didn't have a mom?

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:04.850
Why do we always have to move around?

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.050
Where'd dad go

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:10.150
When he'd take off for days at a time?

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.750
I remember I begged you
-- "Quit asking, Sammy.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.150
Man, you don't want to know."

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.750
I just wanted you to be a kid...

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.750
Just for a little while longer.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.650
I always tried to protect you

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.350
Keep you safe.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.850
Dad didn't even have to tell me.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.650
It was just always my
responsibility, you know?

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.550
It's like I had one job...

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:53.650
I had one job...

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.250
And I screwed it up.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:03.950
I blew it.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.850
And for that, I'm sorry.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.250
I guess that's what I do.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.850
I let down the people I love.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.350
I let dad down.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.650
And now I guess I'm just
supposed to let you down, too.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.550
How can I?

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:42.650
How am I supposed to live with that?

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.750
What am I supposed to do?

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:49.250
Sammy.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:53.550
God.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.450
What am I supposed to do?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.050
What am I supposed to do?!

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:15.850
Come on, already.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.050
Show your face, you bitch!

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:22.150
Easy, sugar. You'll wake the neighbors.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:30.650
Dean.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.250
It is so, so good to see you.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.650
I mean it. Look at you.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.650
Gone and got your family
killed, all alone in the world.

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.050
It's too sweet.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:50.250
Excuse me. You're gonna
have to give me a moment.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.650
Sometimes you got to
stop and smell the roses.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.150
I should send you straight back to hell.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.650
Oh, you should.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.250
But you won't.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.050
And I know why.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.950
Oh, yeah? Yeah.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:08.050
Following in daddy's footsteps,
you want to make a deal.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.550
Little Sammy back
from the dead, and --

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.850
Let me guess, you're
offering up your own soul?

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:16.650
There are a hundred other demons
who'd love to get their hands on it.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:18.750
And it's all yours.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.550
All you got to do is bring Sam back.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.050
Give me 10 years.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.050
10 years, and then you come for me.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.350
You must be joking.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.850
That's the same deal.You
give everybody else.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.550
You're not everybody else.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:38.050
Why would I want to give you anything?

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.250
Just keep your gutter soul.
It's too tarnished, anyways.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.350
Nine years.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.150
No.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:48.850
Eight.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:51.350
You keep going, I'll keep saying no.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.750
Okay, five years.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:58.050
Five years, and my bill comes due.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.450
That's my last offer --
Five years or no deal.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:08.950
Then no deal.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:13.950
Fine. Fine

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.550
Make sure you bury Sam before
he starts stinking up the joint.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:22.250
Wait.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:26.150
It's a fire sale, and
everything must go.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.550
What do I have to do?

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.450
First of all, quit groveling.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.350
Needy guys are such a turnoff.

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:41.150
Look...

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:45.350
I shouldn't be doing this. I
could get in a lot of trouble.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:48.050
But what can I say? I got
a blind spot for you, Dean.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:52.750
You're like a...puppy. You're
just too fun to play with.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.050
I'll do it.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:58.550
You'll bring him back?

00:12:58.850 --> 00:12:59.650
I will.

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:02.250
And because I'm such a saint,

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:05.550
I'll give you one
year and one year only.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:09.750
But here's the thing.

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:14.550
If you try and welch or weasel
your way out, then the deal is off.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:17.450
Sam drops dead. He's back
to rotten meat in no time.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:20.650
So...

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:24.050
Its a better deal
than your dad ever got.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:27.650
What do you say?

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:11.150
Sammy.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.050
Thank god

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:13.950
Hey.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:20.350
Ow.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:21.450
Uh, Dean...

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.750
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, man.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:24.850
I'm just...

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.050
I'm just happy to see you
up and around, that's all.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.750
Come on. Sit down. Okay.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.950
Dean... what happened to me?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:36.550
Well, what do you remember?

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.550
I-I saw you and Bobby, and...

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.650
I felt this pain,
this sharp pain like...

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.550
Like, white-Hot, you know, and...

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.850
Then you started running at me, and...

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:49.350
That's about it.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.450
Yeah, that -- That kid
stabbed you in the back.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.650
You lost a lot of blood. It
was touch and go for a while.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.150
But, Dean, you -- You can't
patch up a wound that bad.

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.250
No, Bobby could.

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:04.650
Who was that kid,anyway?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.250
His name's Jake. Did you get him?

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:07.950
No, he disappeared into the woods.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:09.450
We got to find him, Dean.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.050
And I swear I'm gonna tear
that son of a bitch apart.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:14.150
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy, van damme.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:16.350
You just woke up,all right?

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.550
Let's get you something to
eat. You want something to eat?

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.050
I'm starving. Come on.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:22.850
And that's when you guys showed up.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:24.750
That's awful.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:26.650
Poor Andy.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:30.950
The demon said he only wanted
one of us to walk out alive.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:32.750
He told you that? Yep.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.350
He appeared in a dream.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:36.750
He tell you anything else?

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:40.350
No. No.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:42.050
That was it. Nothing else.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:44.550
You know, what I don't get, Dean,

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:46.450
Is if the demon only wanted one of us,

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.250
Then how did Jake and I both get away?

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.050
Well, I mean, they left you for dead.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.550
I'm sure they thought it was over.

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.950
Now that yellow eyes has Jake,
what's he gonna do with him?

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.150
I don't know.

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:04.850
But whatever it is, we got to stop him.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.850
Hold on, all right? You
need to get your rest.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:08.850
We got time.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:09.850
No, we don't.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:11.850
Sam, oceans aren't boiling, okay?

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.350
Frogs aren't raining from the sky.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.250
Let's get you your strength back first.

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:19.450
Did you call the Roadhouse?
Do they know anything?

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:20.850
Yeah.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.650
Dean...what is it?

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:32.850
The Roadhouse burned to the ground.
Ash is dead, probably Ellen --

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:34.150
A lot of other hunters, too.

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:37.950
Demons?

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:39.150
Yeah, we think so.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.450
We think because ash found something.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:42.550
What'd he find?

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:44.550
Bobby's working on that right now.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.150
Well, come on, then. Bobby's
only a few hours away.

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.950
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Stop.
Sam, stop, damn it.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:55.150
You almost died in there.
I mean, what would I have --

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.850
You just take care of
yourself for a little bit, huh?

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.050
Just for a little bit.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.950
I'm sorry. No.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:22.750
Hey, Bobby. Hey, Bobby.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.150
See you up and around.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:26.650
Yeah, well...

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:28.850
Thanks for patching me up.

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:30.850
Don't mention it.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.050
Well, Sam's better.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.250
And we're back in it now, so...

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:42.150
What do you know?

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:49.750
Well, I found something,but...

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:52.350
I'm not sure what the hell it means.

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:54.750
What is it?

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:59.350
Demonic omens...like a frickin' tidal
wave. Cattle deaths,lightning storms.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.150
They skyrocketed from out of nowhere.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:02.150
Here.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.550
All around here
except for one place --

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.550
Southern wyoming.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.550
Wyoming?

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.250
Yeah.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:13.950
That one area's totally
clean -- Spotless.

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:15.650
It's almost as if...

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:16.650
What?

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:18.850
...the demons are surrounding it.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:20.450
But you don't know why?

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:23.050
No, and by this point,
my eyes are swimming.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:25.350
Sam, would you take a look at it?

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.300
Maybe you can catch
something I couldn't.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:28.450
Yeah, sure.

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:31.550
Come on, Dean.

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.950
I got some more books in the truck.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:35.550
Help me lug them in.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.350
Yeah.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:48.450
You stupid ass! What did you do?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.750
What did you do?!

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:55.850
You made a deal... for Sam, didn't you?

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:58.450
How long did they give you?

00:18:58.750 --> 00:18:59.350
Bobby.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.650
How long?!

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:05.950
One year.

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:08.350
Damn it, Dean.

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:11.750
Which is why we got to find
this yellow-Eyed son of a bitch.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.450
That's why I'm gonna kill him myself.
I got nothing to lose now,right?

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.950
I could throttle you!

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.150
And send me downstairsahead of schedule?

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:28.350
What is it with you Winchesters, huh?

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:29.950
You, your dad,

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:33.450
You're both just itching to
throw yourselves down the pit.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:34.550
That's my point.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:38.200
Dad brought me back, Bobby. I'm
not even supposed to be here.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:42.350
At least this way,something good
could come out of it, you know?

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:43.650
It's like my life can mean something.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.150
What? And it didn't before?

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.050
Have you got that low
an opinion of yourself?

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:50.950
Are you that screwed in the head?!

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:56.650
I couldn't let him die, Bobby.

00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.250
I couldn't.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:01.750
He's my brother.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:05.650
How is your brother gonna feel

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.050
When he knows you're going to hell?

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:12.850
How'd you feel when you
knew your dad went for you?

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.550
You can't tell him.

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:18.150
You take a shot at me,
whatever you got to do,

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.550
But please don't tell him.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:41.550
Ellen?

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.750
Ellen. Oh, god.

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:57.250
Bobby, is this really necessary?

00:20:57.350 --> 00:21:00.150
Just a belt of holy
water. Shouldn't hurt.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.750
Whiskey now, if you don't mind.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.650
Ellen, what happened? How'd you get out?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.950
I wasn't supposed to.

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.950
I was supposed to be in
there with everybody else.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.350
But we ran out of
pretzels, of all things.

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:23.550
It was just dumb luck.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:32.350
Anyway, that's when ash
called, panic in his voice.

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:35.050
He told me to look in the safe.

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:36.450
Then the call cut out.

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:39.950
By the time I got back,
the flames were sky-High,

00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:42.050
And everybody was dead.

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.350
I could n't have been
gone more than 15 minutes.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.050
Sorry, Ellen.

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:49.450
A lot of good people died in there.

00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:51.950
And I got to live.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:54.650
Lucky me.

00:21:57.850 --> 00:21:59.550
Ellen,you mentioned a safe.

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:01.050
A hidden safe we keep in the basement.

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:02.750
Demons get what was in it?

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:03.550
No.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:13.350
Wyoming.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:14.750
What does that mean?

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:19.650
I don't believe it.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:23.350
What? You got something?

00:22:23.850 --> 00:22:25.050
A lot more than that.

00:22:26.950 --> 00:22:30.350
Each of these x's is an
abandoned frontier church --

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:32.350
All mid-19th century

00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:35.250
And all of them built by Samuel Colt.

00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:38.350
Samuel Colt --The demon-Killing,
gunmaking Samuel Colt?

00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:40.650
Yep. And there's more.

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:43.350
He built private railway lines

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:45.550
Connecting church to church.

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:49.950
It just happens to lay out like this.

00:22:51.450 --> 00:22:53.150
Tell me that's not what I think it is.

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:54.650
It's a devil's trap.

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:57.950
A 100-Square-Mile
devil's trap.

00:22:58.050 --> 00:23:01.350
That's brilliant. Iron
lines demons can't cross.

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:02.850
I never heard of anything that massive.

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:03.950
No one has.

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:06.950
After all these years none of the
lines are broken? It still works?

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:08.950
Definitely.

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:10.750
How do you know?

00:23:10.850 --> 00:23:12.550
All those omens Bobby found.

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:14.750
That means the demons, they must
be circling and they can't get in.

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:17.250
Yeah, well... they're trying.

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:18.550
Why? What's inside?

00:23:19.050 --> 00:23:20.150
That's what I've been looking for,

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:24.250
And, uh, there's nothing except an old
cowboy cemetery right in the middle.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.850
Well, what's so important
about a cemetery or...

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:29.450
What's Colt trying to protect?

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:31.750
Well, unless...

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:32.950
Unless what?

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.850
What if Colt wasn't trying
to keep the demons out?

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.650
What if he was trying
to keep something in?

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:40.350
That's a comforting
thought. Yeah, you think?

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:42.150
Could they do it, Bobby?
Could they get inside?

00:23:42.250 --> 00:23:43.250
This thing's so powerful,

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:46.050
You'd practically need
an a-Bomb to destroy it.

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:48.150
No way a full-Blood demon gets across.

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:51.550
No.

00:23:53.150 --> 00:23:54.350
But I know who could.

00:24:26.350 --> 00:24:27.250
Howdy, Jake.

00:24:30.350 --> 00:24:31.650
So, did you have a nice trip?

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:32.750
I'm here.

00:24:32.950 --> 00:24:34.850
I did what you asked. Now what?

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:38.850
50 miles thataway, there's
a cemetery, a crypt.

00:24:38.950 --> 00:24:40.350
You got to open that for me.

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:42.250
Think you can manage that, sport?

00:24:42.450 --> 00:24:44.550
You know what? Screw you
and your freaky orders.

00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:45.550
Go do it yourself.

00:24:45.650 --> 00:24:48.550
Oh, I can't. I can't
go that way -- Not yet.

00:24:48.650 --> 00:24:49.650
Why not?

00:24:52.150 --> 00:24:53.750
I just can't.

00:24:54.150 --> 00:24:57.550
But if you're gonna open that crypt
for me, you're gonna need a key.

00:24:58.050 --> 00:24:58.950
A gun?

00:24:59.050 --> 00:25:01.350
Oh, this isn't just any gun, Jake.

00:25:01.550 --> 00:25:04.550
This is the only gun
in the whole universe

00:25:04.650 --> 00:25:06.550
That can shoot me dead.

00:25:07.650 --> 00:25:09.050
Is that so? Yep.

00:25:09.550 --> 00:25:10.650
Here, take it.

00:25:16.550 --> 00:25:17.450
Oh, my.

00:25:17.650 --> 00:25:20.750
I'm shocked at this
unforeseen turn of events.

00:25:20.850 --> 00:25:23.550
Go ahead, Jake.Squeeze that
trigger. Be all you can be.

00:25:23.650 --> 00:25:25.950
This will all be over. Your
life can go back to normal.

00:25:26.450 --> 00:25:28.550
Of course, the army won't take
you back 'cause you're awol.

00:25:28.650 --> 00:25:32.150
But I'm sure you could get your
old job at the factory back.

00:25:33.250 --> 00:25:34.450
But then, on the other hand,

00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:37.450
The rest of your life and your family's

00:25:37.550 --> 00:25:40.450
Could be money and
honey, health and wealth,

00:25:40.550 --> 00:25:42.750
Every day is ice-Cream sundae.

00:25:42.850 --> 00:25:44.850
And all you got to do
is this one little thing.

00:25:44.950 --> 00:25:45.850
Why me?

00:25:45.950 --> 00:25:49.050
Oh, Jake. It's got to be you.

00:25:49.450 --> 00:25:52.650
I've been waiting for
you for a very long time.

00:25:52.950 --> 00:25:53.850
You're my leader.

00:25:53.950 --> 00:25:56.650
You open that crypt, and
you will have your army.

00:25:56.750 --> 00:25:58.450
You're talking about
the end of the world.

00:25:58.550 --> 00:26:01.150
No, not the end
-- The beginning...

00:26:01.550 --> 00:26:04.350
A better world where your
family will be protected.

00:26:04.450 --> 00:26:05.750
More than that.

00:26:06.650 --> 00:26:07.950
They'll be royalty.

00:26:10.050 --> 00:26:11.850
Buddy boy,you have the chance

00:26:11.950 --> 00:26:14.850
To get in on the ground floor
of a thrilling opportunity.

00:26:14.950 --> 00:26:16.050
What do you say?

00:26:16.250 --> 00:26:17.250
It's your call.

00:26:29.550 --> 00:26:30.650
Attababy.

00:26:57.250 --> 00:26:58.250
Howdy, Jake.

00:27:09.750 --> 00:27:10.750
Wait...

00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:13.450
You were dead.I killed you. Yeah?

00:27:14.350 --> 00:27:15.650
Well, next time, finish the job.

00:27:15.750 --> 00:27:16.850
I did.

00:27:17.750 --> 00:27:20.050
I cut clean through
your spinal cord, man.

00:27:24.250 --> 00:27:25.850
You can't be alive.

00:27:27.950 --> 00:27:29.050
You can't be.

00:27:29.350 --> 00:27:32.250
Okay, just take it real easy there, son.

00:27:32.650 --> 00:27:33.650
And if I don't?

00:27:33.750 --> 00:27:34.950
Wait and see.

00:27:36.550 --> 00:27:38.250
What, you a tough guy all of a sudden?

00:27:38.950 --> 00:27:40.550
What are you gonna
do -- Kill me?

00:27:40.750 --> 00:27:41.650
It's a thought.

00:27:41.750 --> 00:27:43.750
You had your chance. You couldn't.

00:27:44.050 --> 00:27:45.750
I won't make that mistake twice.

00:27:50.350 --> 00:27:52.150
What are you smiling
at, you little bitch?

00:27:54.850 --> 00:27:55.750
Hey, lady.

00:27:57.450 --> 00:27:58.450
Do me a favor.

00:28:00.050 --> 00:28:01.650
Put that gun to your head.

00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:14.450
See, that ava girl was right.

00:28:14.550 --> 00:28:15.450
Once you give in to it,

00:28:15.550 --> 00:28:18.450
There's all sorts of new jedi
mind tricks you can learn.

00:28:18.550 --> 00:28:19.550
Let her go.

00:28:19.850 --> 00:28:21.350
Shoot him.

00:28:21.850 --> 00:28:23.850
You'll be mopping up skull
before you get a shot off.

00:28:26.650 --> 00:28:28.950
Everybody, put your guns down.

00:28:31.050 --> 00:28:32.450
Except you, sweetheart.

00:28:51.550 --> 00:28:52.450
Okay.

00:28:52.950 --> 00:28:53.750
Thank you.

00:29:23.550 --> 00:29:26.150
Please...don't.

00:29:26.850 --> 00:29:27.850
Please.

00:30:00.150 --> 00:30:00.950
Oh, no.

00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:02.150
Bobby, what is it?

00:30:03.450 --> 00:30:04.450
It's hell.

00:30:07.150 --> 00:30:08.250
Take cover
-- Now!

00:30:30.050 --> 00:30:30.750
What the hell just happened?!

00:30:30.850 --> 00:30:33.850
That's a devil's gate,
a damn door to hell!

00:30:41.950 --> 00:30:43.750
Come on! We got to shut that gate!

00:30:53.850 --> 00:30:55.350
If the demon gave this to Jake...

00:30:56.750 --> 00:30:57.650
Then maybe...

00:31:05.450 --> 00:31:07.050
A boy shouldn't play with daddy's guns.

00:31:23.850 --> 00:31:24.850
Dean!

00:31:31.450 --> 00:31:33.050
I'll get to you in a minute, champ.

00:31:33.350 --> 00:31:35.750
I'm proud of you --
Knew you had it in you.

00:31:42.750 --> 00:31:43.750
Sit a spell.

00:31:48.550 --> 00:31:50.150
So, Dean...

00:31:50.550 --> 00:31:52.150
I got to thank you.

00:31:52.350 --> 00:31:55.050
You see, demons can't resurrect people

00:31:55.150 --> 00:31:56.450
Unless a deal is made.

00:31:56.550 --> 00:31:59.050
I know, red tape --
It'll make you nuts.

00:31:59.150 --> 00:32:02.850
But thanks to you,
Sammy's back in rotation.

00:32:03.750 --> 00:32:06.050
Now, I wasn't counting
on that, but I'm glad.

00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:08.150
I liked him better than Jake, anyhow.

00:32:09.950 --> 00:32:10.850
Tell
me --

00:32:10.950 --> 00:32:11.850
Have you ever heard the expression

00:32:11.950 --> 00:32:15.250
"If a deal sounds too good
to be true, it probably is"?

00:32:15.550 --> 00:32:17.250
You call that deal good?

00:32:17.650 --> 00:32:19.950
It's a better shake
than your dad ever got.

00:32:20.450 --> 00:32:23.250
And you never wondered why?

00:32:23.750 --> 00:32:25.150
I'm surprised at you.

00:32:25.950 --> 00:32:26.750
I mean...

00:32:27.550 --> 00:32:30.350
You saw what your brother
just did to Jake, right?

00:32:30.650 --> 00:32:32.750
That was pretty cold,wasn't it?

00:32:35.750 --> 00:32:37.750
How certain are you

00:32:37.850 --> 00:32:42.000
That what you brought
back is 100% pure Sam?

00:32:51.150 --> 00:32:52.649
You of all people should know

00:32:52.650 --> 00:32:55.550
That what's dead should stay dead.

00:32:57.550 --> 00:32:58.350
Anyway...

00:32:59.850 --> 00:33:01.350
Thanks a bunch.

00:33:01.550 --> 00:33:04.050
I knew I kept you alive for some reason.

00:33:04.450 --> 00:33:05.950
Until now, anyway.

00:33:07.650 --> 00:33:08.750
I couldn't have done it

00:33:08.850 --> 00:33:10.950
Without your pathetic, self-Loathing,

00:33:11.050 --> 00:33:13.150
Self-Destructive desire

00:33:13.250 --> 00:33:15.550
To sacrifice yourself for your family.

00:36:00.050 --> 00:36:01.950
Well, check that off the to-Do list.

00:36:03.650 --> 00:36:04.650
You did it.

00:36:05.250 --> 00:36:06.350
I didn't do it alone.

00:36:09.350 --> 00:36:10.750
Do you think dad really...

00:36:12.450 --> 00:36:14.450
Do you think he really
climbed out of hell?

00:36:15.950 --> 00:36:17.350
The door was open.

00:36:20.850 --> 00:36:22.550
If anyone's stubborn enough to do it...

00:36:25.050 --> 00:36:26.050
It would be him.

00:36:31.050 --> 00:36:32.450
Where do you think he is now?

00:36:35.150 --> 00:36:36.150
I don't know.

00:36:38.850 --> 00:36:41.150
I kind of can't believe
it, Dean.I mean...

00:36:42.750 --> 00:36:44.350
Our whole lives,everything...

00:36:45.050 --> 00:36:47.050
Has been prepping for this, and now I...

00:36:51.250 --> 00:36:53.050
I kind of don't know what to say.

00:36:56.850 --> 00:36:57.650
I do.

00:37:07.050 --> 00:37:08.650
That was for our mom...

00:37:10.950 --> 00:37:12.450
You son of a bitch.

00:37:22.150 --> 00:37:23.650
You know, when Jake saw me...

00:37:24.350 --> 00:37:25.750
It was like he saw a ghost.

00:37:30.450 --> 00:37:32.150
I mean, hell, you heard him, Dean.

00:37:33.550 --> 00:37:34.550
He said he killed me.

00:37:37.450 --> 00:37:38.650
I'm glad he was wrong.

00:37:39.050 --> 00:37:40.450
I don't think he was,Dean.

00:37:44.050 --> 00:37:46.750
What happened... after I was stabbed?

00:37:48.650 --> 00:37:50.550
I already told you. Not everything.

00:37:52.950 --> 00:37:54.750
Sam, we just killed the demon.

00:37:56.750 --> 00:37:58.550
Can we celebrate for a minute?

00:38:03.850 --> 00:38:05.050
Did I die?

00:38:05.350 --> 00:38:06.750
Oh, come on.

00:38:07.550 --> 00:38:09.850
Did you sell your soul for
me, like dad did for you?

00:38:09.950 --> 00:38:10.850
Come on! No

00:38:16.050 --> 00:38:17.150
Tell me the truth.

00:38:20.050 --> 00:38:21.350
Dean, tell me the truth.

00:38:21.450 --> 00:38:22.350
Sam...

00:38:33.250 --> 00:38:34.500
How long do you get?

00:38:40.450 --> 00:38:41.450
One year.

00:38:44.050 --> 00:38:45.150
I got one year.

00:38:48.450 --> 00:38:49.750
You shouldn't have done that.

00:38:50.850 --> 00:38:51.850
How could you do that?

00:38:51.950 --> 00:38:53.050
Don't get mad at me.

00:38:55.450 --> 00:38:56.450
Don't you do that.

00:38:58.750 --> 00:38:59.750
I had to.

00:39:00.950 --> 00:39:02.450
I had to look out for you.

00:39:03.850 --> 00:39:04.850
That's my job.

00:39:04.950 --> 00:39:06.650
And what do you think my job is?

00:39:07.150 --> 00:39:07.850
What?

00:39:08.250 --> 00:39:11.450
You saved my life over and over.

00:39:12.050 --> 00:39:13.350
I mean, you sacrifice everything for me.

00:39:13.450 --> 00:39:15.150
Don't you think I'd do the same for you?

00:39:18.350 --> 00:39:19.250
You're my big brother.

00:39:20.350 --> 00:39:23.450
There's nothing I wouldn't do for you.

00:39:27.650 --> 00:39:30.050
And I don't care what it takes.
I'm gonna get you out of this.

00:39:33.750 --> 00:39:35.850
Guess I got to save
your ass for a change.

00:39:37.650 --> 00:39:38.250
Yeah.

00:39:39.750 --> 00:39:40.550
Well...

00:39:41.650 --> 00:39:43.450
Yellow-Eyed demon might be dead,

00:39:43.750 --> 00:39:45.550
But a lot more got through that gate.

00:39:45.750 --> 00:39:46.750
How many, you think?

00:39:47.350 --> 00:39:49.950
100, maybe 200.

00:39:50.250 --> 00:39:51.250
It's an army.

00:39:52.750 --> 00:39:54.250
He's unleashed an army.

00:39:57.250 --> 00:39:58.850
Hope to hell you boys are ready.

00:39:59.550 --> 00:40:01.150
'Cause the war has just begun.

00:40:03.650 --> 00:40:04.750
Well, then...

00:40:14.450 --> 00:40:15.750
We got work to do.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.750
